      "head_commit": {
        "id": "2cde3e6c175be786a41506d54bfab3b28658212b",
        "tree_id": "ea722117274921e101d257ece031200318e782e7",
        "message": "fix(hardening): H2 wave 3e — make two DownloadServiceTests deterministic\n\nBoth were new in wave 1 and had never actually executed green:\n\n- testRapidDuplicateDownloadStartsExactlyOneTransfer assumed an\n  unstructured Task would win the admission race against synchronous\n  caller code; on MainActor the structured call always reserves first and\n  then blocks in waitForCompletion until the gate releases — which sat\n  after the assertions, so the 180s execution-timeout killed the test\n  with no assertion message. Wait until the first transfer has actually\n  reached the transport before firing the duplicate start; refusal is\n  then guaranteed and fast.\n- testRetryFromFailureListReResolvesFreshComponents pointed its completion\n  path at a nonexistent temp file, so the successful manual retry died as\n  validationFailed, and asserted lastFailure was nil even though the prior\n  failed attempt legitimately leaves it set. Give the test the same real\n  temp/destination fixture as its siblings and acknowledge the stale\n  failure banner before retrying so the nil-failure assertion proves the\n  retry itself produced no new failure.",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-22T06:07:17Z",
